  "worked_solution": "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ It doesn't rain.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ Robert goes for a walk.\n\nThe inverse of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\n¬A⇒¬B.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B:$\n\n- $¬A:$ It rains.\n\n- $¬B:$ Robert doesn't go for a walk.\n\nTherefore, the inverse is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If it rains, then Robert doesn't go for a walk.",
